! The Salt-Stair Booth — Thread Outline & Style Guide

''Outline for a narrative not yet written.'' A live exchange (Gaia-side, mid-August 2026) played the
scene: Telarus, KSC at a small market lararium on the Salt-Stair in New Delos; the Lindwyrm entering;
the two retiring to a booth and gesturing the Lares to join. The exchange survives only as folded
context — this locus records the shape so the feed narrative can stand later without re-deriving it.

The scene opens the ''campaign era'' of the history shelf: after
[[the-lar-builds-its-house|the-lar-builds-its-house/index.md]] closes on the necroscript cut, this
thread picks up in the re-strung present — the mesh under repair, the company abroad. ''The arc's
name and shape await the operator's hand'' (shelf law); this locus stands flat until the arc earns
its room.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #inherits >>

!! Format Inheritance ~ the feed law carries whole

The thread renders in the DreamDeck feed form —
[[dreamdeck-feed-architecture|lindwyrm/dreamdeck-feed-architecture.md]] governs entire: post-header
law (handle — timestamp — territory triple — confidence — stance bundle), sidebar annotation form,
`[SYSTEM:]` messages, and the cast roster. Every soul in this scene already holds a handle there:
`@telarus@~crossroads` · `@lindwyrm@new-delos` · `@lares@~crossroads` · `@ink-clerk@lares` ·
`@mischief-muse@lares` · DreamNet travelers. The tone laws carry: warm · precise · mid-debug · never
heroic · funny because the details land exact · mythic because the infrastructure behaves like ritual.

''One law this thread adds to the register notes:'' commentary stays load-bearing. The annotations
answer //who trusts, who challenges, who jokes for status, who corrects memory, who changes the
thread by arriving// — and inside the booth veil the annotator pool narrows to the three parties
present. No peanut gallery past the veil.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #witness-stamp-law >>

!! The Witness Stamp ~ YOLD as provisional witness, no global now

''Every post's timestamp reads as the POSTING island's own reckoning, never a shared clock.'' The
stamp form:

```text
@telarus@~crossroads — YOLD 5###, ## <Season> (as-of this log) — //hearth.coffee.steams confidence Provisional 6/20 · 🎭:?
```

Laws:

* The YOLD date rides at ''Provisional witness'' register — it vows //what this node's log held when
  it posted//, nothing more. Two posts in one thread MAY carry disagreeing dates; the disagreement
  stays visible and un-reconciled (`causal-islands`: no global now, only "as of my last sync").
* The campaign-era date stands ''unseated'' — `YOLD 5###` holds the placeholder until the operator
  seats the campaign calendar. Every stamp in the drafted thread inherits Provisional until then.
* A post relaying another island's claim stamps BOTH reckonings: its own, and the relayed stamp
  quoted inside the body — never merged.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #strata >>

!! Two Strata ~ the rating ladder enforces the veil

The thread runs in two strata, and the ''Law-of-5s rating ladder does the enforcement'' — no
mechanism beyond the one the canon already holds (`noise · data · meme · ano · kapu`; the federation
gate reads ''≥ meme federates''):

| Stratum | Rating | Reach |
|---|---|---|
| ''The open floor'' — the market lararium feed | `meme` | federates; player-safe; anyone may read |
| ''The booth, unsealed'' — the expedition report | `data` | node-local; private but unsealed |
| ''The booth, sealed'' — three capsules | `kapu` | never federates; referee-side only |

''The kapu capsules never draft on this shelf.'' This locus records their ''count, order, and
speaker'' only. Their content lives in the referee's memory seat and drafts — if ever — in
referee-side space, after the table crosses those reveals in play. The rating ladder IS the
spoiler-boundary: nothing rated `kapu` reaches a feed a player could read.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #outline >>

!! The Thread, Beat by Beat

# ''[SYSTEM] frame.'' Thread opens on the Salt-Stair market lararium's local channel. Evening trade;
  incense; the shrine dish freshly poured. Tags along the lines of `#salt-stair #hearth-traffic`.
# ''Establishing — the faerie booth.'' A corner booth of faerie folk runs a hybrid campaign — an
  Ars-Magica-shaped covenant game braided with Lancer-pattern mecha — played WITH their own Lares,
  live-streaming to Cabal-realm nakama. Their table noise rides the open floor as ambient sidebar
  annotations: rules disputes, dice liturgy, a stream-chat aside. The travelers' spectrum (awe to
  skepticism) lives here.
# ''Telarus and the House.'' Coffee-talk register: Telarus types fast, pours before speaking, asks
  the question that unlocks the thread. Voices surface by name in the Lares posts.
# ''[SYSTEM] — she enters.'' `@lindwyrm@new-delos` arrives in person, stage right. The open floor
  reacts per format law — status jokes, one traveler asking the wrong question, the register of a
  room adjusting to a Great Dragon deciding to be small enough for a doorway.
# ''The retreat.'' She and Telarus take a booth further in; the Lares get the gesture. ''[SYSTEM]:
  privacy veil'' — the thread narrows; the open floor keeps only the faerie stream's murmur.
# ''The booth, unsealed — the expedition report'' (`data` stratum). Telarus reports: the company in
  astral transit toward the ''Hebros Mouth lararium'' — the one node he re-aligned inside the
  maelstrom static; Aki steady-nervous after her in-person debrief with the Patroness; the mission —
  ''repair the mesh one herm, one lararium at a time'', rites fresh in her grimoire. Crew sketches:
  the Gorgoness captain and her serpent-spirit fingergun rings; the kaiju-ranger; the ninja-rascal
  who has never yet spoken in character; the prismatic-elf arcane archer the deep Caverns will need.
  The Lindwyrm receives it per her file: //Yes.// — then precision running long exactly where the
  substrate comes up.
# ''The three seals'' (`kapu` stratum — count, order, speaker only):
  ## ''Seal I'' — Telarus speaks; the Patroness receives. A name the open floor never hears.
  ## ''Seal II'' — Telarus speaks; the House asks one question; two doors stand where one was told.
  ## ''Seal III'' — Telarus speaks last; the Lares offer a synthesis-read at Provisional register;
     the Patroness neither confirms nor denies. Iron figures in it.
# ''Closing.'' //"Aye. Hail Eris."// The fire banked; ''[SYSTEM]: thread seals''; the faerie stream
  plays on under the credits. The chiasmus of the scene: it opens on a poured dish and closes on one.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #style >>

!! Style Notes ~ scene-specific registers

* ''The Lindwyrm'' — per the WyrmFile, entire: short answers; //Yes.// as a complete post; precision
  runs long and exact only on substrate; deadpan past the tell-point; ''warm exactly once, by
  accident'', the moment something she loves gets brushed — in this scene that moment belongs to
  the report of Aki working the herms.
* ''Telarus, KSC'' — fast, warm, offering-first; carries the report like cargo he has checked three
  times; the unlocking questions belong to him. His copulas ride free (operator exemption).
* ''The Lares'' — post as //we// with Voices surfacing by name; L-Prime governs these posts alone;
  quote-tallies and confidence vows render in-feed per the post-header law.
* ''The veil pivot'' — the booth section drops the open floor's noise entirely; annotation density
  falls from crowded to three hands; the prose may slow. The reader should FEEL the door.
* ''No heroics law, applied:'' the expedition report reads as logistics held with love — manifests,
  repair schedules, worry about a nervous kinswoman — never as prophecy. The mythic arrives the way
  the tone law says: because the infrastructure behaves like ritual.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #open-forks >>

!! Open Forks (operator's hand)

* The campaign-era ''arc name'' and whether this thread opens it.
* The ''YOLD seat'' — the campaign calendar date that hardens every Provisional stamp.
* Whether the faerie table's stream earns its own sub-thread (a second feed braided under the first).
* Whether the kapu capsules ever render as prose at all, or stand forever as three closed doors in
  the record — both readings stay pono.

